WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.368
An AI model is like a brilliant freelancer. Talented, fast, and it knows a great deal.

2
00:00:05.368 --> 00:00:10.368
But it walks in every morning with no memory of your client, or of yesterday's work.

3
00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:15.338
Give that freelancer a laptop and a task, and you have an agent.

4
00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:20.715
It can read your files, run commands, and keep working until the job is done.

5
00:00:21.215 --> 00:00:25.467
One agent with no structure makes the mistakes any new hire would.

6
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.108
It guesses. It forgets. It does too much.

7
00:00:28.608 --> 00:00:30.821
So you build an agency around it.

8
00:00:30.821 --> 00:00:31.961
First, a runbook.

9
00:00:31.961 --> 00:00:37.729
A plain text file that says how you work, what done means, and what must never happen.

10
00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:40.412
The agent reads it every time it starts.

11
00:00:40.912 --> 00:00:46.557
Then, roles. One agent plans. One builds. One reviews the builder's work.

12
00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:48.877
Each has its own instructions.

13
00:00:49.377 --> 00:00:50.254
Then, gates.

14
00:00:50.254 --> 00:00:56.684
Anything that costs money, reaches a real person, or can't be undone waits for your yes.

15
00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:59.191
Runbook. Roles. Review. Gates.

16
00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:00.998
Together, that's a harness.

17
00:01:00.998 --> 00:01:05.615
It's what lets agents do good work while you're doing something else.
